{
 "id": "HT-PR-01 (prune: a dry run lists old evidence and deletes nothing; --apply keeps every handoff file, summary copy, MANIFEST, ledger and the evidence a newer handoff cites, marks the rows it removed pruned; read-only folders are never written)",
 "layer": "H",
 "owner": "skills",
 "note": "0.1.6 PRUNE (owner 2026-11-08: a handoff folder should not hold a lot of data, and a later clean-up must not delete the small handoff files). `prune` lists evidence/<stem>/ folders and dated disposable folders older than the age (default disposable_keep_days, else 14 days) and at least --min-mb, with the bucket and the handoff or summary copy each belongs to. --apply deletes only the files listed: never a handoff .md (a .md in a unit with kind handoff included), a summary copy, MANIFEST.tsv, ledger.md, or a file a handoff newer than the age cites (its MANIFEST row, or its path in the text); a young handoff's folder (its restart recipes) is never old enough. Rows of deleted copies become scan `pruned`, which verify reports as `pruned`, not `missing`. The old default folders and --root folders are listed read-only. A stale --plan is refused.",
 "now": "2026-11-08T12:00:00+03:00",
